## 2026-06-22 — design locked (from README + formal.egg + data-format probes)

Semantics confirmed:
- Iteration(src, symbol, rest, body): group src by head PathItem; per group bind
  symbol:=head (a 1-item path), rest:=set-of-tails (a space); eval body; UNION groups.
  This is MORKL's structural eliminator / "for each".
- TailsUnion = existential head-projection; TailsIntersection = universal; Head = heads.
- Restriction x<|p = x ∩ (p·Σ*); canonical law: x <| Singleton p = Wrap p (Unwrap x p).
- Composition = concat product; Wrap p s = Singleton p · s; Unwrap strips known prefix.
- formal.egg gives the full meaning-preserving law set (ring laws, distributivity,
  wrap/unwrap cancel, product/singleton=wrap, tails laws, restriction canonical form).
  These are the SC's deterministic simplification (transient-reduction) rules; MORKL's
  `Lower.*` already implements most as Scala `subs` rewrites — I will reuse + extend.
- Recursion intent (README §4.7/§7.2/§9): routines are least fixpoints via self-Call;
  `fixpoint` helper = `last \/ step(last \/ f(last))`; GOAL transforms: (a) tail-rec
  `r(a)=x(a) \/ r(g(a))` -> imperative loop; (b) NAIVE datalog -> SEMI-NAIVE (accumulate
  + frontier delta, keep 3 of 4 joins). These are the prize supercompilation outcomes.

SC architecture (positive supercompilation, specialized to the set algebra):
  configuration = Space term with free SpaceMention/PathRef as input vars; routine env
  ambient. drive = simplify-to-normal-form (egg/Lower laws) then unfold outermost Call
  (incl. SELF calls — the key difference from Routine.optimized). whistle = homeomorphic
  embedding on Space/Path AST; generalize via msg (anti-unification) -> abstract differing
  subterms into fresh routine params. fold = renaming/instance match against ancestor ->
  tie knot to residual routine. residualize process tree -> Set[Routine]; verify by
  eval-agreement with the original on the example data.

Data loaders planned:
- lot.metta: relations hasName/hasId/male/female/parent. (parent P C)->parent.P.C +
  child.C.P; (female X)->female.X. Build same shape as AuntQuery.context -> aunt query.
- carac: rules are a Scala DSL in src/test/.../graphs/*.scala (RecursivePath = TC on
  a->b->c->d; Acyclic = two-hop; TopSort = TC on 17-edge DAG). Reproduce as MORKL.
- fred.rle: header `x=20,y=20,rule=B3/S23`; body b/o/$/! run-length -> live (x,y) set
  -> Cell.x.y paths. GoL step = 8-neighbour B3/S23.
- NOAA .nc: HDF5; python h5py available (ncdump absent). anom[time,z=1,lat36,lon72],
  fill -999.9, lat 5° -87.5..87.5, lon 2.5..357.5. Extract latest slice via h5py ->
  bucketize -> binary-trie prefix paths like the existing temperature test.

Next: implement SC matching layer (alpha-renaming, instance match, homeomorphic
embedding, msg) in src/main/scala/Supercompiler.scala + unit tests; compile green.

