[2026-06-27] INCREMENT 5: MUTUAL-RECURSION LOWERING (plan §5.5 — the headline). New lowerMutualSCC:
lowers a parameter-passthrough mutually-recursive SCC (≥2 routines) to a SINGLE Space.Fixpoint via
the tagged-union encoding — combine the SCC relations into one tagged relation S = ⋃_i tag_i·r_i
(tag_i = "#scc#<name>"), replace every passthrough SCC-call r_j(params) by Unwrap(S, tag_j), take the
least fixpoint of the combined body from ∅, and project each routine as r_i(params)=Unwrap(fixpoint,
tag_i) (now NON-recursive -> inlinable). lowerCalls now groups recursive routines into mutual-
reachability SCCs and lowers each lowerable one; lowered SCC routines become acyclic and inline.
PRECONDITIONS (else honest residual): identical (refs,mentions) signature across the SCC; every
SCC-call passes parameters through unchanged (arg-changing recursion stays residual — defunctionalize
is out of scope); STRUCTURAL MONOTONICITY (no SCC-call under a Subtraction/Raffination subtrahend, or
under Range/Fold/residual/grounded) so the ascending Kleene chain from ∅ reaches a least fixpoint.
The overlay contexts (increment 3) are load-bearing here: the combined Fixpoint body references both
the outer params and the fixpoint variable.
VERIFIED (GraphExecT): degenerate f(x)=x∪g(x),g(x)=x∪f(x) -> single Fixpoint, eval==evalI==execT==x,
no residual; non-degenerate intersection-bounded A(u)={a}∪(B(u)∩u),B(u)={b}∪(A(u)∩u) over {a,b,c} ->
A=B={a,b} across all backends; arg-changing f->g(x("h")) correctly STAYS residual. No regressions:
non-Slow 161/0; SCDegeneracies 1000 progs 0 failures 23.4%; CorpusValidation 1000x1000; ExDatalog TC
sound; ExNQueens n=12=14200; ExGameOfLife fusion.
SCOPED HONESTLY: mutual recursion is LOWERED to a single Fixpoint and evaluated via the existing
(naive Kleene) Fixpoint executor. Semi-naive / delta evaluation (plan §7.2) is NOT yet implemented;
arg-changing (defunctionalized) mutual recursion is NOT lowered. Both are clear follow-ups.

