bridge (real transpileZ output / real optimised DAG as shared Tr lets, observed through Reflect
against the reference literal); instance smt legs on folded sides at the observation paths.

HARD-WON ENGINEERING FINDINGS (all documented in-file):
- eager reference in egg: BIREWRITES (assoc/comm closure, Wrap un-fusion) are combinatorial at
  program scale — replaced by DIRECTED canonicalisation + ruleset scheduling (acu separated); the
  remaining distribute rules descend one level per seminaive round top-down, so literals emit as
  BALANCED trees (log-depth); egglog has no early exit → runner uses an ascending ROUNDS ladder
  (convergence window can sit below an explosion threshold, e.g. converge@12 explode@16).
- movement spec is an OBSERVATION calculus, not an evaluator: virtual-Restriction observations over
  deep eager instances are out of reach (cost model held); eager instance evaluation belongs to the
  impl recursion (bridge) / formal reference.
