================================================================================
2026-08-05  Path-LENGTH bounds: two-tier analysis (Lower.lenBounds + LenZ3)
================================================================================
The length twin of the size analysis, same architecture and dominance contract.

TIER 1 — Lower.lenBounds (MORKL.scala, next to sizeBounds): compositional interval
`∀ p ∈ eval(s): lo ≤ |p| ≤ hi` over ALL constructs. The statement is ∀-quantified, so any
interval is vacuously sound for an empty space; `lo > hi` is the canonical provably-empty marker
(LenBounds.empty) and COMPOSES: min/max at unions (an empty operand's (INF,0) marker drops out),
max/min at meets (a crossing marker = provable length-emptiness), saturating + at compositions.
Transfers: union hull; intersection max/min; subtraction/raffination/range = left/src;
restriction lo = max(lo_x, lo_prefixes) (a kept path HAS a prefix in y); composition/wrap = sum
(wrap ≡ Singleton(p)·src); unwrap/tails = shift down (ε-only source ⇒ tails empty); iteration
AND fold = body bounds with rest ↦ tail-lengths of src (both output ⋃ per-group body evals; a
src with hi=0 has no heads ⇒ empty); fixpoint = hull(init, body); mention/call/grounded
unknown. pathLenBounds(p) gives path-expression intervals; pathItemLen generalized to honor ANY
lengthHint (was ==1 only) — hints are trusted contracts.

TIER 2 — LenZ3 (LengthConstraints.scala): per hash-consed node lo/hi/emp variables + a unary
define-fun `len_i(l)` OVER-APPROXIMATING the node's length set, keeping the DISJUNCTIVE
structure the hull loses: literals/singletons emit exact length sets (≤64 distinct, else
interval), meets conjoin child predicates, wrap/unwrap/tails SHIFT the child predicate when the
prefix length is exact. Witnesses: ¬emp ⇒ the extreme lengths satisfy len_i and the baseline
interval (dominance by construction). Emptiness: structural TRUE-direction facts (union/comp/
wrap exact; ⇒-only elsewhere) + cross-facts from sizeBounds (hi=0 ⇒ emp; lo≥1 ⇒ ¬emp); the
objectives run under ¬emp_root (bounds are vacuous for ∅; unsat ⇒ provably empty ⇒ baseline).
Soundness model: every reality induces a model with true extremes/emptiness (binder vars read
as GLOBAL extremes over all bindings, the argmax-witness idea from SizeZ3), so min lo_root /
max hi_root are outer bounds. Macro discipline: define-funs expand exponentially under DAG
sharing (x∪x doubles per level; the pooled fuzzer builds exactly that) — nodes whose estimated
expansion exceeds 50k degrade to their interval predicate (cost 1). Reuses SizeZ3's
alphaRename/scopesProblem/children/runZ3/Status (relaxed to private[morkl]); ground-fold twin
seeds exact length sets for closed nodes (same closedness + size≤200k budget).

MOTIVATING EXAMPLE (LenBoundsCheck): ((({len10} ∪ {len25}) ∩ {len15}) ∪ {ε}) x {len2, len3·len3}.
The meet's predicate (l=10 ∨ l=25) ∧ (l=15) is UNSAT ⇒ emp forced ⇒ union collapses to {ε} ⇒
composition pinned to the right factor: z3 [2, 6]. The hull baseline can only say [2, 21]
(meet hulls to [15,15] since 15 ∈ [10,25]). Verified BOTH closed (ground-foldable) and OPEN
(len-25 free path variable via lengthHint — pure constraint reasoning, no fold possible).

VALIDATION (LenBoundsCheck, 4 tests green): the example closed+open; transfer pins (wrap shift,
unwrap, tails −1, ε-only tails empty, restriction prefix lower, iteration head+tail, empty
composition, hinted variable exact); corpus gate — 5000 closed instances: every path length
inside closed AND open baseline intervals; 200 open corpus programs through LenZ3: 200 solved,
0 scope limits, dominance everywhere, 1000 random-input soundness checks clean. z3 strictly
tighter than baseline on only 1/200 corpus programs — expected: fuzzed literals draw lengths
1-2, so hulls are already tight; the z3 win is length-disjoint meets (the example shape).
Regression: SizeBoundsCheck, SizeZ3Check, AlgebraicLaws, ProductUnionCheck, CorpusLawValidation
(100k) all green after the pathItemLen generalization.

================================================================================
2026-08-06  SPATIAL TYPES: length-indexed count abstract interpretation (input -> output)
================================================================================
The unifying tier above the size and path-length analyses: abstract a Space as a LENGTH-INDEXED
COUNT domain (per path-length count interval), from an input environment to an output type.
SpatialTypes.scala: Ivl (count interval), SpaceType(byLen: SortedMap[len, Ivl], rest, restLens),
SpatialEnv(spaces: Map[SpaceMention, SpaceType], paths: Map[PathRef, LenBounds]).

WHY IT UNIFIES: the two projections ARE the existing analyses --
  SpaceType.size = sum of the per-length intervals  (domain of Lower.sizeBounds / SizeZ3)
  SpaceType.len  = the support hull                 (domain of Lower.lenBounds / LenZ3)
Keeping counts PER LENGTH is what neither can express alone, e.g. a restriction by a length-3
prefix set ANNIHILATES the length-2 class (a path cannot start with a longer prefix) while
leaving longer classes, and TailsUnion then shifts survivors down by exactly one item.
`rest == Ivl.zero` means the support is exactly byLen's keys (closed) -- the informative case.

TRANSFERS (each a true cardinality fact): union pointwise [max lo, lo+hi]; intersection per-class
min (a class present on only one side => 0, so length-disjoint meets are PROVABLY EMPTY);
subtraction relu; restriction kills classes shorter than the shortest prefix; RAFFINATION keeps
short classes EXACTLY (they can never be restricted away); composition = per-class-pair
convolution, upper = sum of products over pairs, lower = MAX over pairs (different (a,b) pairs
with a+b=L can collide, so no summing; within one pair concat is injective for a fixed side);
wrap = exact class SHIFT (bijection); unwrap/tails = shift down; iteration/fold = scaled union of
the body type with rest |-> tails-of-src and the head sym bound to LENGTH EXACTLY 1 (always true,
a real precision win from the lengthHint work); fixpoint = Kleene iteration with count widening
plus a POST-FIXPOINT CHECK (F(T) subset-of T => lfp subset-of T; unverified => widen to
lenBounds-with-unbounded-counts). Widening keeps <=24 classes / lengths <=8192 by spilling to
`rest` (only loosens). Supersedes the partial otypes/itypes experiment (which is ??? at
TailsUnion/Fixpoint) with a total, sound analysis; otypes left in place, not deleted.

VALIDATION (SpatialTypeCheck, 4 tests green):
 - input->output example: xs : {len2 |-> K, len4 |-> N, len6 |-> M}, ys : size 0, k : len 3;
   \/(xs <| (ys \/ {k})) infers EXACTLY {len 3: [0,N], len 5: [0,M]}, len-1 class annihilated,
   size hi = N+M, len [3,5] -- matches the requested upper type. Ground truth on a matching
   instantiation is {3 |-> N, 5 |-> M}. NOTE: the sound LOWER bound is 0 per class, not 1: nothing
   in the declared input types says xs's long paths actually start with k, so the restriction may
   filter everything. Getting lower 1 needs a "the restriction is non-vacuous" premise.
 - control-flow s||g: reproduces the derivation exactly. s={} => size [3,3] AND the per-length
   classes of g exactly; s nonempty (2 paths) => [2,5]. Both never looser than Lower.sizeBounds.
 - per-length precision: wrap shifts classes as a bijection, unwrap shifts back, length-disjoint
   meet provably empty, raffination exact on short classes, tails dedupe [1, N].
 - 3000 closed corpus instances: per-length counts SOUND (both closed and open-with-env forms);
   strictly tighter than tier-1 on size 1308/3000 and on length 60/3000.

CROSS-VALIDATION vs BOTH z3 TIERS (150 corpus programs): length projection within LenZ3 on
150/150; size projection within SizeZ3 on 148/150. The analyses are INCOMPARABLE by design and
the 2 outliers show why (reported, not hidden):
   #21  spatial [0,20] vs z3 [0,15]  -- z3's inclusion-exclusion |a∪b| = |a|+|b|-|a∩b| on
        overlapping union operands; a per-length count domain cannot see sibling overlap.
   #130 spatial [0,inf) vs z3 [1,inf) -- z3's subset saturation proves nonemptiness through
        `(x <| x)` shapes; spatial's per-class lower stays 0.
Both were CONSISTENT with spatial everywhere (asserted), i.e. both sound. Resolution:
SpatialTypes.bestSize/bestLen return the MEET of spatial ⊓ tier-1 ⊓ z3, which dominates each by
construction (asserted) and is the answer a consumer should use; meet soundness re-checked on 40
closed programs. Regression: LenBoundsCheck, SizeBoundsCheck, SizeZ3Check, AlgebraicLaws,
CorpusLawValidation, CorpusValidation green.

NOT YET DONE (deliberate): no dependent/relational information (the {min,max,avg}E(P"v") degree
queries need per-key counts, i.e. indexing classes by head as well as length) -- the natural next
tier, noted as requested.

================================================================================
2026-08-06  Spatial-type LATTICE formalized: 42 FOL/SMT obligations, all PROVED
================================================================================
Formalized the spatial abstract interpretation and certified it: scripts/gen_spatial_obligations.py
-> proofs/spatial/*.smt2 (42 files) + proofs/spatial/REGISTRY.tsv (43 rows, no orphans either way);
wired into proofs/run.sh as a new family; docs/design_spatial_lattice.md enumerates every property
used, every law, and its verdict; atlas.md S9 rewritten to cover the three analyses (size, path
length, spatial types) incl. the two files it predated (LengthConstraints.scala, SpatialTypes.scala).

RESULT: 42/42 PROVED (z3), of which vampire independently proved 19 -- all the pure-FOL sp_*
concretion files except sp_tails_shift / sp_comp_collision / sp_isprefix_len. Default-mode vampire
has no theory portfolio, so on the datatypes+arithmetic lat_* half it predictably times out and z3
is the prover of record (documented in run.sh and traps.md); budgets are 15s lat_* / 60s sp_*.

LAYER lat_* (20 files) -- THE LATTICE. Counts are N u {inf} as a DATATYPE (inf a real top, not a
sentinel Int); intervals over it ordered by inclusion; a spatial type is a pointwise-indexed family.
Proved: Cnt total order; ⊑ a partial order; join/meet ARE lub/glb; ⊥/⊤; idempotence/commutativity/
absorption; DISTRIBUTIVITY; saturating +/x/relu- laws (incl. "0 beats inf" and monotone-DOWN in the
subtrahend); MONOTONICITY of every per-class transfer (binary/unary/scale, the scale case lifting a
separately-certified nonlinear Int core); per-transfer local soundness; MEET-DOMINATES (the
bestSize/bestLen theorem); widening soundness; projection monotonicity; pointwise type order/join;
and the POST-FIXPOINT theorem (F#(T) ⊑ T and init ⊑ T => every Kleene iterate ⊑ T, via an explicit
nat-induction schema) -- the theorem the Fixpoint transfer actually rests on.

COUNTERMODEL FOUND (a real catch, not a formality): the first draft asserted [0,0] is the lattice
bottom; z3 returned SAT. gamma([0,0]) = {0} is NOT a subset of gamma([2,5]), so [0,0] is an ORDINARY
element ("this class is empty") and ⊥ is the INCONSISTENT interval (inf, 0) -- exactly the
LenBounds.empty marker the code already used. lat_ivl_bounds now proves the corrected statement AND
the refutation of the old one. (Second, smaller catch: the ⊥ conjunct needs an okc guard, else a
negative-count interval refutes it.)

LAYER sp_* (22 files) -- THE CONCRETION, over the same set-of-paths denotation as proofs/laws plus
len. Proved: len(append) additivity and isPrefix => len <= (induction schemas); RESTRICTION
ANNIHILATES classes shorter than the shortest prefix; RAFFINATION KEEPS those classes EXACTLY;
restriction/raffination PARTITION x; length-disjoint sets have EMPTY meet; wrap is an injective
length-shift (into) producing nothing else (onto); unwrap/tails shift down with >=1 tail per
nonempty class; composition adds lengths with a witnessing pair and is injective for a fixed left
factor; the COMPOSITION COLLISION theorem (ground witness: {a}.{aa} and {aa}.{a} both yield a.a.a)
-- why the per-class lower bound must be a MAX and never a sum; iteration keys have length exactly
1; the subsumption family; SELF-RESTRICTION x <| x = x and x \| x = {} (isPrefix reflexive); the
per-class union/inter/sub bounds; inclusion-exclusion strictly beats the additive bound on overlap;
and the Galois connection (c in gamma(alpha c), alpha . gamma ⊑ id).
The CARDINALITY BRIDGE is 4 standard finite-set axioms (inclusion-exclusion, meet ⊆ both, x\y = x
minus meet, non-negativity), asserted explicitly and marked DEFINITIONAL; everything on top is
proved, nothing else assumed.

THE PAYOFF -- three certified law families became code (SpatialTypes.scala):
  * subsumes(x,y): syntactic ⊆ (∩/∖/<|/\| ⊆ left operand; operands ⊆ union; transitive) driving
    relational cases -- y ⊆ x => x∪y = x, x∩y = y, x∖y = {} when x ⊆ y. Kills the double counting
    on x ∪ (x∩y), the exact shape where SizeZ3's relational facts beat the spatial analysis.
  * partitionOf: (x<|y) ∪ (x\|y) = x EXACTLY, per class (the per-length analogue of SizeZ3's
    partitionPair).
  * self-restriction identities.
Also fixed a precision bug the formalization exposed: an unknown-LENGTH Singleton was typed [0,1]
when a singleton always holds EXACTLY one path (boundedExact), and TailsUnion's spill bucket can
promise >=1 tail when every length in it is headed.
MEASURED: strictly tighter than tier-1 on 1480/3000 closed corpus instances for size (was 1308) and
87 for length (was 60). All 5 SpatialTypeCheck tests green (a new one pins the relational cases);
regression LenBoundsCheck / SizeBoundsCheck / SizeZ3Check / AlgebraicLaws / CorpusLawValidation green.

HONEST LIMITS (documented in design_spatial_lattice.md S7, unchanged by this work): no per-class
MEET variable, so sibling overlap needs syntactic subsumption to be visible -- SizeZ3 stays strictly
tighter on 2/150 corpus programs (bestSize meets both, so consumers lose nothing); the single spill
bucket loses per-class headedness (a loHeaded component would recover it); widening is proved SOUND
but its termination argument is structural, not certified.

