STOP-SHIP CONFIRMED AND FIXED. The reviewer's reproducer is real: on
  Composition(Composition(lit(25 distinct lengths), same), lit{eps, len 12})
12 of 61 length classes violated their UPPER bounds (len 24: actual 36 vs claimed [1,25]).
ROOT CAUSE exactly as diagnosed: the representation invariant is "rest counts the paths at lengths
NOT in byLen", and `at(l)` answers from the tracked class alone for a tracked l -- but nothing ever
enforced that `restLens` excludes the tracked keys. Composition routes every rest-involving product
into the spill while the tracked class keeps only the tracked x tracked convolution, so the tracked
class omitted real paths. Unsound, not imprecise.
FIX: SpatialTypes.disjoin, applied in `build` (hence after every transfer) and in a new public
`widen` -- any tracked class the spill range covers is folded INTO the spill, combining lowers with
`max` (if the buckets did overlap, the two claims may describe the same paths, so only the max is
guaranteed) and uppers with saturating `+`. Precision is lost only where widening had already given
up; terms under the caps are unaffected. Also: SpaceType.of/closed bypassed normalize, so the
documented 24-class cap did not hold -- both now route through `widen`.
NEW GATES (src/test/scala/SpillSoundness.scala): the reviewer's reproducer; 19 widened-operator
cases (composition both sides/self, union, intersection, subtraction both directions, wrap, unwrap,
tails-union/intersection, restriction, raffination, range, iteration, nested iteration, and two deep
compositions); >MaxLen paths; the class-cap check; 60 randomised spill/track collisions. Every case
checks per-length bounds, both projections, AND the representation invariant itself.

