FIXPOINT: the review says the transfer needs concrete monotonicity. I do not think that is the gap:
with upper-envelope-monotone transfers (lat_transfer_mono_*) and local soundness, each iterate is
bounded without any monotonicity of the Zippy body. The REAL gap was that the concrete fixpoint
returns the UNION of all iterates, and `join`'s per-class upper ADDS counts, so a finite-count
candidate can only be a post-fixpoint when the body contributes nothing -- previously that held only
as a side effect of the widening schedule (widenCounts at k>=2). It is now REQUIRED explicitly:
`unionClosed(t) = join(t, F#(t)).within(t)`, and a finite candidate that fails it is widened and
re-checked before acceptance. Accidental soundness replaced by a checked condition.

