Bringing it up surfaced four genuine must/may leaks, all the same family — an operation that can
DELETE members leaking MUST information through one of its channels:
  1. inter(a, top) returned `a`, keeping must-heads an intersection may remove;
  2. restrict treated a MAY-present epsilon in the prefix set as absent, returning empty for a
