  Restriction(Composition(Literal({d}), Literal({d})), Literal({b,d}))   eval={d.d}  inferred=∅
Root cause: `Composition` degraded to an OPEN head set, and `restrict` keyed its result on
`x.heads.keys ∩ prefixes.heads.keys` while marking it CLOSED because the PREFIX side was closed — so
an untracked head of `x` equal to a prefix head was dropped. Fixed by keying on the CLOSED side and
descending through `x.under(h)`. Certified as a refutation: gsem_l1_restrict_openkeys_unsound.

`SpatialType` is the REDUCED product with the histogram, reduced in both directions after every
transfer. Real transfers now: literal, singleton (incl. unknown path of bounded length), union,
inter, sub, restrict, raffination, wrap/wrapUnknown, unwrap/unwrapUnknown, tailsUnion, tailsInter,
composition (grafts at the leaves — was ⊤), range, iteration/fold PER HEAD GROUP, fixpoint (a
certified post-fixpoint — was ⊤), call (interprocedural — was ⊤). ⊤ only for: Grounded*, an absent/
active Call, unwrap by an unbounded path, an undeclared Mention, an uncertified Fixpoint, budget
